netinet/arp_rtrequest
	arp_rtrequest() and arprequest() of sys/netinet/if_ether.c on the
	life of one route, in two phases, then RTM_DELETE as the teardown.
	Phase 1 is a new route, RTM_ADD or RTM_RESOLVE, on an arbitrary
	gateway sockaddr (sa_len 0..255, any family, any sdl_nlen and
	sdl_alen, laid out as rt_setgate leaves it: exactly ROUNDUP(sa_len)
	bytes, at the end of a 264 byte object) and arbitrary rt_flags.
	Phase 2 (optional) is RTM_CHANGE as route_output does it: maybe a
	new arbitrary gateway, the flags in RTF_FMASK except RTF_MPLS
	toggled, then arp_rtrequest(RTM_ADD) again on the same route.
	VERIFIED: no out-of-bounds access (the 6 byte memcpy from enaddr
	in arprequest), no leak, and after each phase the invariant that
	arplookup, arpresolve and arpcache rely on: when RTF_LLINFO is set
	or rt_llinfo is not NULL, the gateway is AF_LINK, sa_len >=
	sizeof(struct sockaddr_dl), sdl_alen is 0 or ETHER_ADDR_LEN and
	offsetof(sdl_data) + sdl_nlen + ETHER_ADDR_LEN <= sa_len.  The
	flag, not only rt_llinfo, is checked because route_output sets
	RTF_LLINFO for every AF_LINK gateway before the hook runs and
	passes userland's flags through, so it holds for every route,
	also those arp_rtrequest returns early for (RTF_GATEWAY,
	RTF_BROADCAST, RTF_MULTICAST, RTF_MPLS, RTM_ADD of RTF_CLONING).
	RTM_RESOLVE clears RTF_CLONING, RTF_CONNECTED and RTF_STATIC, as
	rtrequest does for a clone.  Eight mutants, all VIOLATED:
	mutant_prefix/, mutant_prefix2/, mutant_prefix3/ (the sources
	before e3dbf8882, 96dde7faa and 569b20305), and, built from the
	current source, mutant/ (no "+ ETHER_ADDR_LEN" room),
	mutant_noclr/ (RTF_LLINFO not cleared for a rejected gateway),
	mutant_nodel/ (existing llinfo not deleted), mutant_noearly/ and
	mutant_nocloning/ (RTF_LLINFO not cleared on the early-return and
	RTF_CLONING paths).  Not covered: the arplookup change of
	12a68fffb; rtalloc and rtable_iterate are not modelled.  Native:
	CLEAN; on mutant_prefix the seed in native/seeds reaches the ASan
	heap over-read in arprequest at once.  Check phase about 2 s.

