netinet/tcp_pulloutofband
	tcp_pulloutofband(so, urgent, m, off) of sys/netinet/tcp_input.c
	on a chain of up to 2 mbufs (internal, cluster or read-only
	cluster, any m_len), packets up to 24 bytes, off in 0..plen-1 and
	urgent in 1..plen-off (the caller's guarantee, tcp_input.c 1878,
	1925), followed by the caller's m_adj(m, off).  Real: the function,
	m_adj and the mbuf code.  VERIFIED: no panic; t_iobc is the byte at
	off + urgent - 1 and TCPOOB_HAVEDATA is set; bytes before it stay,
	bytes after it move down by one (one arbitrary byte tracked); the
	sum of m_len drops by exactly 1.  m_pkthdr.len is left unchanged
	(asserted); after m_adj it exceeds the chain by exactly 1.  No later
	reader of this chain depends on it: sbappendstream, tcp_reass and
	tcp_flush_queue use m_len and tlen.  The socket, inpcb and tcpcb
	are static: CBMC_NEW objects count as leaks under
	--memory-leak-check.  Mutants VIOLATED: the memmove length one
	short, m_len > cnt as >=, cnt without its -1 (panic reached).
	Native: CLEAN.  Check phase about 220 s, 355,000 variables
	(timeout 600).

netinet/tcp_reass
	tcp_reass() and tcp_flush_queue() of sys/netinet/tcp_input.c on a
	queue of 0..2 entries and one new segment (0..8 bytes each, one or
	two mbufs, header in the first mbuf's buffer), arbitrary 32 bit
	rcv_nxt, offsets 1..5 (entries) and 0..20 (new) above it, on the
	mbuf contract models; pool_get fails arbitrarily, sbappendstream
	is a model that checks what it is given.  VERIFIED: the queue
	invariant before and after (order, no overlap, th_reseqlen ==
	chain length, entries above rcv_nxt); delivery (chains contiguous
	from the old rcv_nxt, rcv_nxt advances by the delivered length,
	TH_FIN returned exactly when the last delivered chain had FIN, one
	tracked byte); every stream position held before is held once
	after; both pool_get failure paths; the queue limit of a57fe03c6
	(t_segqlen >= max(TCP_REASS_MAXQLEN, sb_hiwat / 1024): a segment
	not at rcv_nxt is dropped, the queue, t_segqlen and rcv_nxt
	unchanged; otherwise t_segqlen is the queue length plus the
	entries beyond the modelled ones, 0 after a flush); no leak or
	double free.  Not
	covered: the byte of a position left in a queued entry, more than 2
	entries, the window.  Mutants VIOLATED: the back-trim overlap one
	too large, the front trim one short, the insertion comparison moved
	by one, the limit test as >, one t_segqlen-- removed.  SEQ_GT ->
	SEQ_GEQ in the insertion is not detected: it
	changes only which of two entries at one sequence number survives.
	tcp_subr.c is included, not in sources: as a separate source its
	copies of header static inlines (counters_inc) cannot be named in
	nobody.  Native: CLEAN.  Check phase about 5 to 7 minutes, 810,000
	variables, --sat-solver cadical (timeout 600).

netinet/tcp_update_sack_list
	tcp_update_sack_list() of sys/netinet/tcp_input.c on a list of 0..6
	SACK blocks (live ones above rcv_nxt, stale ones at or below it) and
	a segment of 1..64 numbers that is old (ends at or before rcv_nxt)
	or new (starts above it), the two kinds the caller passes
	(tcp_input.c 1945-1977).  VERIFIED: after the call 0..6 blocks,
	each non-empty and above rcv_nxt, separated by gaps (touching
	blocks are merged); block 0 is the hull of the segment and the
	blocks it overlaps or touches; the other blocks are the untouched
	old ones, unchanged and in order; no covered number is lost except
	the oldest block of a full list.  rcv_nxt is the constant -16 (wrap
	and zero inside the blocks) and the list is in sequence order: a
	symbolic rcv_nxt or list order timed out.  Not covered: other
	rcv_nxt, lists whose arrival order differs from sequence order, a
	segment of length 0 (SEGMIN 0: natively block 0 is then empty, see
	FINDINGS).  Mutants VIOLATED: the merge test with SEQ_LEQ, the
	count test rcv_numsacks <= MAX_SACK_BLKS.  Native: CLEAN.  Check
	phase about 10 s, 98,000 variables.

netinet/tcp_sack_holes
	tcp_del_sackholes() then tcp_sack_option() of sys/netinet/
	tcp_input.c (the order of tcp_input.c 867, 878) on the sender's
	SACK scoreboard: 0..3 holes built by arithmetic, arbitrary snd_una,
	snd_max, th_ack and one SACK block.  VERIFIED, an invariant both
	keep: holes ordered, disjoint, in [snd_una, snd_max]; start < end
	except that the head may be empty; start <= rxmit <= end; last end
	< rcv_lastsack <= snd_max; snd_numholes == length for a non-empty
