	tcp_del_sackholes, rcv_lastsack not updated on append.  The live
	count assertions are CBMC only: natively replace does not apply to
	pool_get and pool_put.  Native: CLEAN.  Check phase about 700 s,
	480,000 variables, --sat-solver cadical (timeout 1500).

net/pfsync_input
	pfsync_input() of sys/net/if_pfsync.c, the framing of a pfsync
	packet: 0..44 bytes of arbitrary content (the IP header already
	stripped, hlen 0: the function only m_adj()s it away), one or two
	mbufs, ttl arbitrary, at most six subheaders.  The handlers are
	models that assert their buffer is readable for mlen * count bytes
	and mlen is at least their message size; when the harness writes
	the pfsync header (length 0..63), they also assert that what they
	get lies within the declared length.  m_pullup is the harness's own
	model (fresh bytes, no copies; the contract model's copies ran out
	of memory), the softc reference is counted.  VERIFIED: no
	out-of-bounds access, no leak, references balanced.  mutant_prefix/
	(before d415e63fa: a header length below 20 drove m_pkthdr.len negative)
	and mutant/ (the remaining-length test loosened by one) are VIOLATED
	on the declared length, mutant_mlen/ on the message size.  Cover
	and check phase about 8 minutes each, 1.3 million variables, half
	of it symbolic execution (timeout 1800).

