udf/vget
	udf_vget() of sys/isofs/udf/udf_vfsops.c on one file entry block
	of 512 arbitrary bytes; bread, brelse, udf_allocv and the hash
	are models, bcopy is a contract (both ranges, the first 216
	bytes copied).  VERIFIED: no access outside the block or
	u_fentry; on success the fixed part of the entry's type and
	l_ea + l_ad bytes after it lie inside u_fentry.  Check about
	155 s.  mutant_prefix/ is the source before 9a103f788 (l_ea +
	l_ad summed in an int, unchecked: VIOLATED); mutant_sizeonly/
	checks only that int sum against the block, as first proposed
	(VIOLATED: the sum wraps, e.g. l_ea + l_ad == 0xffffff28).

udf/vget_eq
	Refinement: the current udf_vget() against the one before
	9a103f788 (extracted into old_vget.h), on the same block and the
	same bread, M_NOWAIT and udf_allocv outcomes.  VERIFIED: an
	entry that fits in the block, or one with an invalid tag, gets
	the same result (EINVAL where it was ENOMEM for an invalid tag);
	on success the same bcopy from the block and the same vnode
	type, and u_fentry is hdr + l_ea + l_ad bytes (it was 216 +
	l_ea + l_ad).  A valid tag with an entry larger than the block
	gets EINVAL and everything taken is released.  The old function
	is not run on that entry (its bcopy overruns the block).
	mutant_strict/ (>= in udf_fentry_sizes), mutant_alloc/ (the old
	allocation size) and mutant_leak/ (no pool_put on rejection) are
	VIOLATED.

udf/mountfs
	udf_mountfs() on a medium of arbitrary content (at most 5 breads
	per run; bread hands out arbitrary bytes of the size asked).
	udf_find_partmaps and udf_vat_get are models, so the partition
	map parsing is not covered.  VERIFIED: no access outside an
	object, no division by zero, bread sizes in (0, MAXBSIZE], no
	leak; on success um_bsize is a power of two in [DEV_BSIZE,
	MAXBSIZE] with matching um_bmask and um_bshift, and the root file
	entry passes udf_vget's checks (otherwise the mount cannot be
	looked up through, hence not unmounted).  mutant_prefix/ is the
	source before 9a103f788 (VIOLATED: um_bsize, descriptor reads
	past a small block, the metadata file entry's l_ea, the root
	read's size, um_stbl leaked on failure).  mutant_noroot/ is the
	source before f61f24bf6 (VIOLATED: the root entry).  The leak
	check counts any allocation not freed by the end, so the harness
	frees what udf_unmount frees after a successful mount.

ext2fs/ext4_find_extent
	ext4_ext_find_extent() of sys/ufs/ext2fs/ext2fs_extents.c on an
