ext2fs/ext4_bmapext, ext2fs/ext4_bufatoff, ext2fs/ext4_ext_read
	The callers of ext4_ext_find_extent(), one target per file (each
	file includes ufs/inode.h, which has no include guard), with
	ext4_ext_find_extent replaced by a model of its contract (above):
	NULL with path untouched, or an earlier path->ep_bp released and
	then NULL or path with ep_bp and ep_ext each set or not.
	The extent returned lies in the held buffer if there is one, else
	in the inode, with arbitrary content.  ext4_ext_read also has the
	extent cache as a model and at most 3 breads.  VERIFIED: no access
	outside an object (nor to a released buffer), no buffer held on
	return but the one ext2fs_bufatoff hands back.  mutant_prefix/ is
	each file before a8b853ca1 (VIOLATED: ext4_bmapext used an
	uninitialised path; all three returned holding path.ep_bp;
	ext4_ext_read used a stale ep_ext, in a released buffer, after a
	failed lookup).  ext4_bufatoff/mutant_release/ is ext2fs_subr.c as
	of a8b853ca1, which read ep after releasing the buffer it points
	into (VIOLATED; fixed in 6eb817310).
	Since ea2c5c7ef they also check holes: every data read of the device
	is lbn's block in a written extent that contains lbn, and
	ext4_bmapext returns -1 or such a block.  ext4_ext_maps is
	defined in the harnesses as in ext2fs_extents.c; ext4_ext_read
	has models of ext2fs_size and uiomove and a cache model that
	holds only extents mapping their block.  mutant_holes/ is each
	file before ea2c5c7ef (VIOLATED: a hole, or an unwritten extent, read
	the blocks after the previous extent).

ext2fs/search_dirblock, ext2fs/search_dirblock_diag
