ext2fs/readdir, ext2fs/readdir_size
	ext2fs_readdir() on 32-byte directory blocks of arbitrary content
	from an arbitrary offset (lseek, seekdir); VOP_READ, uiomove and
	strncpy are models.  readdir (getdents length up to 96):
	VERIFIED: no panic, ufs_dirbad never called (the offset comes from
	the user), no access outside the buffer, every name copied lies
	in the bytes read, uio_offset does not move backwards.
	readdir_size (getdents length up to INT_MAX, the read fails):
	VERIFIED: malloc(9) is not asked for more than MALLOC_MAX.
	mutant_prefix/ is the file before c4c826265 (VIOLATED: readdir reads
	headers past the buffer and names outside the bytes read;
	readdir_size reaches the malloc panic).  readdir/mutant_dirbad/
	reports bad entries through ufs_dirbad (VIOLATED: a read-write
	mount panics on a user-chosen offset).  Without --no-simplify:
	with it CBMC 6.8 fails an invariant on __CPROVER_havoc_slice.
